# Tailwind class constants via `cn`

In `variants.ts`, define reusable Tailwind class strings with `cn(...)` so long lists stay readable across lines. Do not pack everything into one single-line string.

Import `cn` from the package-local helper (`./cn`, `$lib/utils/cn`, or `@company-of-heroes/ui/cn`).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — one dense string (hard to scan / edit)
export const pageShell =
	'border-secondary-800 relative mx-auto flex min-h-screen max-w-6xl flex-col border-x bg-gray-950/80';

// ✅ GOOD — split logical groups with cn
import { cn } from './cn'; // or $lib/utils/cn / @company-of-heroes/ui/cn

export const pageShell = cn(
	'relative mx-auto flex min-h-screen max-w-6xl flex-col border-x',
	'border-secondary-800 bg-gray-950/80'
);
```

## Rules

- Prefer `cn('…', '…')` over template literals or `+` for joining static class chunks
- Group related utilities per argument (layout, then color/border, then state variants)
- Short single-purpose strings may stay as a plain string (`export const interactive = 'cursor-pointer disabled:cursor-not-allowed'`)
- Still use `cn(base, conditional, class)` at call sites when merging; this rule is about **defining** the shared constants

## IntelliSense

Workspace settings enable Tailwind autocomplete inside `cn` / `clsx` via `tailwindCSS.classFunctions`. Prettier sorts classes in those calls via `tailwindFunctions`. Use `cn(...)` for long constants so autocomplete works — plain string exports do not.
